                occupied.remove(spot_id)
    return sorted(occupied)

Before the loop, the set is empty: capacity is ignored then because the lot can never be full with no cars parked. For each enter, the two conditions together enforce that the car is only added when room allows and the spot is free; for each exit, the removal happens only when the spot was occupied. The final return sorts the set into a list of strings, which meets the requirement of a sorted list of spot IDs. Operations on other spots are unaffected by this one, so the state of the set grows and shrinks according to the whole event sequence.

