There are three phases in a full cycle, named in the same order as the duty values, and cycle repeats them indefinitely. For each phase the code appends the label to the list for every tick within the range offset to offset + offset. When the list reaches length n_ticks it stops, so if n_ticks is large or the duty values are short, later phases never begin.

