The point p lies inside the triangle or on one edge when it is on the "inside" side of each of the three edges of the triangle. The inside side of an edge formed by two points v1 and v2 can be determined by the sign of the cross product of v2 - v1 with p - v1; in this context, I mean the cross product of the two vectors as a signed scalar.

