rate_limiter_allowed deals with a non-decreasing list of arrival times, in the order they were received. A request arriving at time t is allowed when the number of earlier or equally recent arrivals with timestamps strictly greater than t - window and at most t is at most limit. The result must be a list of booleans, one per timestamp.

The critical observation is that the window slides as each request enters the picture, so keeping a running window is sufficient. Here's the loop:

