The reachable floors are the floors from start_floor onward in the sweep direction, stopping short when the opposite edge is met. Starting from 1 upwards, those are 1, 2, 3, and so on up to top_floor; starting from 10 downwards, they are 10, 9, 8 down to 1. For each such floor, the program records the floor only if it appears in requests. The order of the output is the order of visits, with the first check starting at start_floor.

